  ],
  "solution": "<p><strong>1.</strong> The two equal strips have width 1 and sample heights <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></math>, since <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&#x0003C;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x0003C;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>. Thus <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo></mrow></math>.</p><p><strong>2.</strong> The exact area is the sum of two triangles on either side of the vertex: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math>.</p><p><strong>3.</strong> Put <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo></mrow></math>. The excess condition is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>. Therefore <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math> or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>, both inside the original interval.</p><p><strong>4.</strong> The requested product is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></math>, answer B. For either value the estimate is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math> and the true area is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></math>, independently checking the excess.</p>"
